    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**El Topo** (1970) revolutionized midnight cinema and established Alejandro Jodorowsky as surrealism's wild prophet. This acid western follows a black-clad gunslinger through a hallucinatory desert quest, mixing Buddhist philosophy with Christian symbolism and shocking violence. Its success at New York's Elgin Theater created the midnight movie phenomenon, paving the way for cult classics like **Eraserhead** (1977) and **The Rocky Horror Picture Show** (1975). John Lennon was so impressed he convinced Beatles manager Allen Klein to distribute it, leading to wider recognition of avant-garde cinema."
      },
