      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's influence extends deep into modern cinema's experimental edges. **Beyond the Black Rainbow** (2010) and **Mandy** (2018) echo its psychedelic violence and mystical themes. Directors like Guillermo del Toro and Nicolas Winding Refn cite El Topo as a major influence, with its fearless mixing of genres and unflinching artistic vision. Even mainstream films like **Django Unchained** (2012) draw from its revisionist western imagery."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "El Topo's production was as legendary as the film itself. Jodorowsky used real rabbits for death scenes, made actors stay in character for days, and allegedly didn't fake any of the film's violence. This commitment to authenticity influenced later maverick filmmakers like Werner Herzog, whose **Fitzcarraldo** (1982) and **Aguirre, the Wrath of God** (1972) similarly pushed boundaries between filmmaking and reality. SUBHEAD: Legacy and Impact on Modern Cinema"
      },
      {
