            "slug": "Jodorowsky's controversial debut feature about a couple's surreal journey to a mythical city",
            "poster": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/iMN4CydHfJ6h9os7gALUomRrdZV.jpg",
            "initialStreaming": "Criterion",
            "tmdb_id": 33257,
            "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/iMN4CydHfJ6h9os7gALUomRrdZV.jpg"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's DNA can be found in everything from **Pan's Labyrinth** (2006) to **A Field in England** (2013). Its blend of western tropes with spiritual questioning influenced **Dead Man** (1995) and **The Good, the Bad, the Weird** (2008). Modern filmmakers like Panos Cosmatos and Ben Wheatley continue mining El Topo's psychedelic territory, proving its lasting impact on boundary-pushing cinema."
      }
